From: AX6 lifecycle review
Subject: [PATCH] ssdk: reject conflicting SD publication and preserve PHY on FAL failure

SD borrows callback providers: equal pointers and NULL contributions are
compatible, but a conflicting live provider is not a replacement lease.
Check the complete typed vector before publishing any contribution. Callers
must still serialize initialization and keep providers alive for all readers;
this is not a concurrent reader drain or a global UK/SD owner coordinator.

If FAL cleanup refuses or fails, its dependents have not been certified as
retired. Keep PHY metadata and driver state available for the caller's retry.
Do not turn an error report into permission to release a lower dependency.
The void module-exit path and the earlier FAL/UK ordering remain separate.

Read-only admission is also checked before outer FAL/PHY initialization.
Invalid device cleanup cannot stop global controls. No reader drain implied.

--- a/include/sal/sd/sd.h
+++ b/include/sal/sd/sd.h
@@ -77,6 +77,8 @@
 		sd_reg_mii_mdio_set(a_uint32_t dev_id, a_uint32_t reg_addr,
 				a_uint8_t value[], a_uint32_t value_len);
 	/*qca808x_start*/
+	/* Read-only admission; not a provider lease or concurrent reservation. */
+	sw_error_t sd_init_check(a_uint32_t dev_id, const ssdk_init_cfg *cfg);
 	sw_error_t sd_init(a_uint32_t dev_id, ssdk_init_cfg * cfg);
 
